###  http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#deaf_community_secrecy_stereotype
:deaf_community_secrecy_stereotype rdf:type :BackgroundKnowledge ;
                rdfs:label "Deaf Community Secrecy Stereotype"@en ;
                rdfs:comment "The meme plays on the trope that members of a club or group are secretive about their existence or rules, often humorously referred to as 'the first rule of [club name]... you do not talk about [club name]'. This trope is used here to imply that deaf people are secretive about their community, which is a harmful stereotype as it misrepresents the openness and visibility of the deaf community."@en ;
                :extractionMethod "llm_extraction_huggingface" ;
                :extractedFrom "90826.png" ;
                :extractionTimestamp "2025-12-19T17:13:38.848568" .

